WEBVTT

00:01.940 --> 00:11.820
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:09.630 --> 00:11.360
We will proceed as stated.

00:12.430 --> 00:13.580
It definitely won't be easy.

00:14.540 --> 00:15.700
Proceed with caution.

00:16.380 --> 00:19.820
Our ninja corps pledge eternal loyalty to you.

00:20.250 --> 00:22.170
Glory to Kagetomo-sama!

00:22.520 --> 00:23.700
Glory!

00:24.880 --> 00:26.250
Watch me,

00:26.840 --> 00:27.450
Hanzo...

00:32.220 --> 00:37.930
Welcome to the Ninja Village!
The Legend of the Hero Gekkouga!!

00:38.970 --> 00:48.820
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

00:38.970 --> 00:48.820
Z

00:40.430 --> 00:41.180
Gekogashira.

00:43.140 --> 00:44.730
The food is ready.

00:46.690 --> 00:52.400
During his quest to get his eighth badge, Satoshi takes a lunch break with his friends.

01:00.540 --> 01:01.830
What's the matter, Gekogashira?

01:07.830 --> 01:08.790
Excellent!

01:10.040 --> 01:11.800
Sanpei! Gekkouga!

01:12.340 --> 01:15.300
We approached you stealthily when we saw you,

01:15.630 --> 01:20.180
but who would've thought Gekogashira would notice our presence? It really has grown.

01:21.100 --> 01:23.640
It's been a while. I'm glad to see you!

01:23.930 --> 01:24.980
Likewise.

01:27.690 --> 01:29.860
We just finished making lunch, so...

01:30.190 --> 01:31.610
...let's eat together!

01:32.070 --> 01:33.320
I be very obliged to you.

01:38.070 --> 01:39.030
The Ninja Village?

01:39.660 --> 01:45.200
That be right. We be on our way home to participate in tomorrow's festival.

01:45.620 --> 01:48.710
What kind of place is the Ninja Village? Are there lots of ninja?

01:49.170 --> 01:54.630
Such be a matter of course. The villagers and the Pokémon be training hard every day.

01:55.130 --> 01:57.970
Uh... And... Uh...

01:57.970 --> 01:58.720
What about kunoichi?

01:59.140 --> 02:00.930
Of course there be beautiful kunoichi too.

02:01.430 --> 02:03.260
Whoa! I'd love to go there.

02:03.560 --> 02:06.180
A ninja festival, huh? That would be great to see.

02:06.520 --> 02:08.190
Yeah, it sounds fun.

02:09.650 --> 02:11.940
Then I will gladly take you there.

02:12.480 --> 02:13.570
Right, Gekkouga?

02:15.230 --> 02:16.360
Now that that's decided,

02:16.610 --> 02:17.900
leave it to me!

02:20.700 --> 02:21.990
Eureka is here!

02:38.470 --> 02:38.930
What's the matter?

02:40.720 --> 02:41.140
Mountains.

02:41.890 --> 02:42.220
Rivers.

02:47.640 --> 02:49.770
Sanpei, welcome back!

02:50.850 --> 02:51.900
I'm back!

02:52.520 --> 02:53.940
Are those friend of yours?

02:54.270 --> 02:54.520
Yes!

02:54.900 --> 02:57.240
The others will be happy too. All right, go.

02:57.490 --> 02:57.900
Certainly.

03:00.820 --> 03:02.700
So it's inside a cave.

03:03.070 --> 03:04.080
It's pitch-dark...

03:04.080 --> 03:05.540
You will be much astounded when you see it.

03:07.870 --> 03:09.660
Whoa!

03:10.000 --> 03:11.460
Awesome!

03:11.870 --> 03:14.750
Welcome. This be the Ninja Village.

03:18.630 --> 03:20.630
Heave-ho!

03:19.880 --> 03:20.630
Everyone!

03:21.680 --> 03:22.510
I be back!

03:23.760 --> 03:24.930
It's Sanpei!

03:25.140 --> 03:26.760
Hey, it's Sanpei!

03:26.970 --> 03:30.140
Ippei, Nihei! Sanpei has come back!

03:35.730 --> 03:37.650
Sanpei, I'm glad you've made it back safely.

03:37.860 --> 03:41.360
Brother Nihei, brother Ippei, I be glad you seem well.

03:41.950 --> 03:44.030
So your Keromatsu has evolved into Gekkouga.

03:44.370 --> 03:45.700
It has become quite potent.

03:47.160 --> 03:48.620
Sanpei, who are these people?

03:49.160 --> 03:50.710
They be my friends.

03:51.080 --> 03:52.210
I'm Satoshi.

03:52.420 --> 03:53.880
This is my partner Pikachu.

03:54.130 --> 03:55.040
And this is Gekogashira.

03:57.500 --> 03:59.170
Nice to meet you. I'm Serena.

03:59.510 --> 04:00.670
I'm Eureka.

04:00.920 --> 04:02.090
This little one is Dedenne...

04:02.340 --> 04:03.300
...and this is Squishy.

04:03.550 --> 04:05.050
I'm taking care of them!

04:06.680 --> 04:09.390
I am Citron, Eureka's brother. Nice to meet you.

04:10.020 --> 04:11.430
Thank you for helping out our brother.

04:11.930 --> 04:13.810
I'm Sanpei's older brother, Ippei.

04:13.810 --> 04:15.770
I'm Nihei; let's get along.

04:16.190 --> 04:16.560
Yeah!

04:18.610 --> 04:20.990
Sanpei's friends are our friends.

04:21.690 --> 04:23.860
I, Hanzo, welcome you too.

04:25.030 --> 04:25.530
Chieftain!

04:26.120 --> 04:27.280
I have just returned!

04:28.530 --> 04:32.710
Good job. Saizo has told me about your devotion.

04:33.080 --> 04:33.750
Sir Saizo did?

04:42.840 --> 04:45.090
Correct. He told me about Satoshi-kun and the others too.

04:45.430 --> 04:46.550
I see.

04:47.050 --> 04:49.060
Hey, hey, what's a "chieftain"?

04:49.390 --> 04:50.430
It means "leader".

04:50.770 --> 04:51.810
The most important person here?

04:52.230 --> 04:53.310
Awesome!

04:53.770 --> 04:57.310
No, no, no, now you're exaggerating.

05:01.440 --> 05:04.110
Geez... Are you all right, chieftain?

05:04.110 --> 05:07.280
Oh, sorry, sorry. I've got to hand it to you, Shinobu-chan.

05:07.280 --> 05:09.410
Maybe I got a cold or something...

05:12.620 --> 05:14.040
It be the ninja art of body replacement.

05:14.620 --> 05:15.790
Awesome!

05:17.460 --> 05:20.800
I'm the chieftain's errand girl, Shinobu. Nice to meet you.

05:20.800 --> 05:23.510
I've decided! I'll keep Shinobu-san!

05:23.510 --> 05:23.760
Whoa!

05:24.920 --> 05:26.880
Have my brother, s'il-vous-plaît!

05:29.510 --> 05:34.020
Shinobu-san, you're the perfect wife for my big brother! Eureka gives you a warm welcome!

05:34.020 --> 05:34.430
Oh my.

05:34.430 --> 05:35.810
Stop it, Eureka!

05:36.520 --> 05:37.520
But...

05:37.520 --> 05:38.270
Thank you!

05:39.020 --> 05:40.310
You may not see it,

05:41.480 --> 05:44.900
but I often look younger to others...

05:46.150 --> 05:48.660
The truth is, Shinobu-chan is 100 years old.

05:49.700 --> 05:50.990
Oh, I'll cancel.

05:53.080 --> 05:54.080
What an honest child.

05:55.450 --> 05:57.040
Kunoichi are amazing...

05:57.460 --> 06:00.540
All right then, Sanpei, show us the results of your studies right away.

06:00.840 --> 06:02.750
Battle me, Sanpei!

06:03.090 --> 06:03.420
Okay!

06:12.810 --> 06:16.140
Nihei-san is the second best ninja, right?

06:16.560 --> 06:19.270
Sanpei said he was the most powerful after Ippei-san.

06:20.900 --> 06:21.520
Please,

06:21.770 --> 06:22.320
Fushigibana!

06:25.570 --> 06:26.530
A Fushigibana, huh?

06:29.280 --> 06:30.820
Fushigibana, the Seed Pokémon.

06:31.450 --> 06:37.290
By spreading the broad petals of its flower and catching the sun's rays, it fills its body with power.

06:37.290 --> 06:39.040
I wonder how it'll battle.

06:40.330 --> 06:42.840
All right, come, Sanpei! I won't go easy on you!

06:43.130 --> 06:44.380
Bring it on!

06:44.960 --> 06:46.670
Gekkouga, Double Team!

06:51.840 --> 06:53.720
Aim at their feet! Vine Whip!

06:58.810 --> 07:00.480
Fushigibana, Razor Leaf!

07:02.810 --> 07:04.150
Do the Water Shuriken!

07:07.780 --> 07:08.440
Gekkouga!

07:08.690 --> 07:09.450
Do the Night Slash!

07:17.500 --> 07:18.500
All right!

07:18.500 --> 07:19.830
Good job, Gekkouga!

07:21.000 --> 07:24.290
Well I'll be... Its speed and power are incomparable with before.

07:24.630 --> 07:26.170
You've become strong, Gekkouga.

07:31.130 --> 07:32.430
Go on the offensive at a breath!

07:32.760 --> 07:34.260
Gekkouga, do the Night Slash!

07:35.260 --> 07:37.060
Use the ninja art of seclusion with Petal Blizzard!

07:42.690 --> 07:43.980
Now, use Razor Leaf!

07:54.030 --> 07:55.830
Gekkouga, stand!

07:58.410 --> 08:00.040
Fushigibana, Solar Beam!

08:10.760 --> 08:11.300
Gekkouga!

08:12.220 --> 08:12.760
That's enough!

08:13.510 --> 08:14.840
Hang in there!

08:15.050 --> 08:15.760
Gekkouga!

08:20.730 --> 08:23.310
We were no match for my brother, huh?

08:23.640 --> 08:24.230
That's right.

08:25.520 --> 08:27.980
You two still have many openings.

08:28.320 --> 08:32.820
You should've been able to decide the battle with the first Night Slash.

08:35.450 --> 08:37.030
What do you mean?

08:37.830 --> 08:38.830
Didn't you notice...

08:39.370 --> 08:43.580
...how skillfully Fushigibana blocked right before Night Slash hit?

08:47.170 --> 08:48.590
I had no idea.

08:49.340 --> 08:53.300
We contained the damage to a minimum and waited for a chance to turn the tables.

08:54.510 --> 08:56.680
So that's the prowess of the number two...

08:57.470 --> 09:02.890
That said, fighting against Fushigibana, who you had a disadvantage against, on such an even level is excellent.

09:03.310 --> 09:05.560
You've grown, Sanpei.

09:05.810 --> 09:06.810
Thank you very much.

09:07.350 --> 09:10.690
It's obvious that you've been training together with Gekkouga a lot.

09:10.980 --> 09:12.860
Keep it up.

09:13.240 --> 09:13.690
I will!

09:20.450 --> 09:24.870
Hm... To think the ninja boy's home was in a place like this...

09:25.460 --> 09:30.170
Besides Gekkouga and Fushigibana, there seem to be a lot more skilled Pokémon here too.

09:30.170 --> 09:34.840
If we get them, we could form a ninja unit for the Rocket Gang!

09:35.300 --> 09:38.300
I see. We'll increase our offensive capabilities with ninja power!

09:38.640 --> 09:41.850
That way we could easily take control over the Kalos region as well.

09:41.850 --> 09:45.350
Let's get absolutely all of them. This has become interesting.

09:45.560 --> 09:49.980
Let's show our prowess to the ninja of this village!

09:49.980 --> 09:51.070
Yeah!

10:03.290 --> 10:04.040
Let's begin.

10:04.450 --> 10:04.870
Understood!

10:11.340 --> 10:12.420
Pokémon Quiz!

10:12.840 --> 10:13.840
The answer is...?

10:30.520 --> 10:33.730
It's like a secret base. So exciting!

10:34.940 --> 10:37.360
So you made use of a natural cave to make this house.

10:37.650 --> 10:40.360
It looks like you could live here comfortably.

10:41.740 --> 10:43.280
This be my room.

10:44.200 --> 10:46.410
Come on, no need to restrain yourself. Come in!

10:47.080 --> 10:48.960
Huh, it looks surprisingly normal.

10:51.290 --> 10:53.750
Ah, it be good to be home for once.

10:59.680 --> 11:00.680
It's a Keromatsu!

11:01.680 --> 11:03.260
So you took this before you set off.

11:03.970 --> 11:05.930
Right. It was a photo to commemorate the event.

11:06.970 --> 11:10.440
I was aiming to become the number one Pokémon user in the village.

11:10.940 --> 11:13.310
But I could not best brother Nihei.

11:13.730 --> 11:16.530
It be obvious I thus cannot hold a candle to brother Ippei either.

11:17.230 --> 11:19.280
I still lack training.

11:20.110 --> 11:22.950
Sanpei, what will you do from now on?

11:23.660 --> 11:26.040
I shall once again devote myself to my studies here in the village...

11:26.540 --> 11:28.290
...while helping out my brothers.

11:28.830 --> 11:29.870
"Help out"?

11:30.250 --> 11:33.500
The truth is, brother Ippei is going to become chieftain on this occasion.

11:34.000 --> 11:34.960
The chieftain?

11:35.380 --> 11:39.260
At the end of tomorrow's festival, Sir Hanzo will retire.

11:39.800 --> 11:44.760
From now on, it will mainly be the three of us who will protect the village.

11:45.050 --> 11:47.640
I see. Do your best, Sanpei, Gekkouga.

11:48.560 --> 11:48.770
We will.

11:51.190 --> 11:53.100
We can't fall behind either, Pikachu.

12:07.330 --> 12:08.240
Dedenne?

12:09.540 --> 12:10.750
Squishy?

12:11.160 --> 12:12.160
Huh?

12:13.250 --> 12:14.120
Dedenne?

12:14.500 --> 12:15.460
Squishy!

12:15.460 --> 12:17.040
What's the matter, Eureka?

12:17.500 --> 12:18.050
Don't tell me...

12:22.760 --> 12:23.930
In a place like this...?!

12:23.930 --> 12:27.600
They might have entered this secret passage.

12:28.180 --> 12:29.350
I have to go, quick!

12:29.640 --> 12:31.140
Eureka, that is dangerous!

12:31.810 --> 12:34.060
Sanpei, what does it look like down there?

12:34.810 --> 12:35.480
Citron!

12:38.690 --> 12:39.650
Let's go too!

12:39.650 --> 12:39.980
Yeah!

12:56.880 --> 12:58.130
Whoa!

12:59.710 --> 13:00.670
Whoa!

13:06.930 --> 13:08.510
I knew you would be here.

13:08.850 --> 13:10.600
I be glad we found you.

13:10.600 --> 13:12.850
I see, they came from your room.

13:13.480 --> 13:15.980
Geez, I was worried!

13:16.310 --> 13:18.400
That is my line...

13:22.610 --> 13:23.900
What is this place?

13:25.570 --> 13:27.280
A place like this inside a <i>cave</i>...?

13:27.700 --> 13:30.450
This is a shrine dedicated to the heroes of the village.

13:30.780 --> 13:31.450
Heroes?

13:31.740 --> 13:33.450
That's right. Let me show you.

13:46.180 --> 13:47.010
These are...

13:49.720 --> 13:50.970
...Pokémon, right?

13:52.850 --> 13:55.060
The heroes of the village are Pokémon?

13:55.390 --> 13:55.730
Yes.

13:56.480 --> 14:00.860
According to legend, a battle between ninja broke out in this village in ancient times.

14:01.230 --> 14:03.570
What? Ninja fought ninja?

14:03.980 --> 14:04.940
But why?

14:04.940 --> 14:05.940
Who knows?

14:06.570 --> 14:08.320
At this point we no longer know the reason behind the conflict,

14:08.780 --> 14:12.030
but it was apparently these guys that fought to protect the village back then.

14:12.790 --> 14:15.830
Among those Pokémon, this Gekkouga seemed to be the leader.

14:17.250 --> 14:21.880
The truth is, I chose Keromatsu as my partner out of admiration for this hero.

14:22.590 --> 14:26.550
I raised Keromatsu and evolved it into Gekogashira, then Gekkouga.

14:27.010 --> 14:29.130
To tell you the truth, it be the same for me.

14:30.930 --> 14:34.060
But that Gekkouga looks a bit strange, doesn't it?

14:35.470 --> 14:36.520
You think so...?

14:47.990 --> 14:50.280
You're polishing that very carefully.

14:54.490 --> 14:57.410
This is no more than some mere decoration.

14:58.040 --> 15:01.460
What truly matters is having the trust of the people of the village.

15:01.960 --> 15:04.290
But Ippei will do fine.

15:05.960 --> 15:06.800
Delicious!

15:07.010 --> 15:09.970
Shinobu-chan, your tea is always the greatest!

15:10.800 --> 15:12.090
Thank you very much.

15:18.270 --> 15:19.100
Nice.

15:19.390 --> 15:22.350
Let's cause a disturbance and gather all the Pokémon in the village square!

15:22.560 --> 15:26.570
And then we'll get all of them. Our plan is perfect!

15:26.900 --> 15:28.530
Let's get to work!

15:37.290 --> 15:37.740
Hey...

15:38.160 --> 15:38.870
What's going on?

15:54.470 --> 15:55.350
Airmd?

15:58.850 --> 16:00.020
What's going on?!

16:05.730 --> 16:06.940
Huh, what?

16:06.940 --> 16:07.980
It's the alarm!

16:08.610 --> 16:09.780
Something happened outside!

16:10.150 --> 16:10.610
Let's go check.

16:11.150 --> 16:14.570
Listen, Sanpei. You take Satoshi-kun and the others to the chieftain.

16:14.870 --> 16:15.700
Understood.

16:16.160 --> 16:16.780
This way!

16:16.780 --> 16:17.240
O-Okay!

16:45.980 --> 16:46.440
Nihei!

16:46.610 --> 16:47.980
Nobody's hurt, I hope?

16:48.270 --> 16:49.480
No, everyone's fine.

16:51.190 --> 16:53.360
Brother, how do you judge the situation?

16:58.580 --> 17:00.040
They have been disciplined well.

17:00.450 --> 17:03.120
They're not wild Pokémon. Who is behind this?

17:03.460 --> 17:06.380
I don't know. All of a sudden they came flying and attacked us...

17:09.880 --> 17:10.340
They're coming!

17:10.840 --> 17:12.170
I'm counting on you, Gekkouga!

17:14.420 --> 17:14.930
Chieftain!

17:15.880 --> 17:16.930
Oh, Sanpei.

17:17.180 --> 17:19.600
We have been instructed to wait here by my brothers!

17:42.120 --> 17:44.620
Who are you guys?

17:45.290 --> 17:47.370
Hanzo, chieftain of the Ninja Village,

17:48.130 --> 17:49.960
we've come to take you.

18:05.480 --> 18:06.440
Hanzo-san!

18:09.270 --> 18:10.610
Wait, you guys!

18:10.980 --> 18:12.440
Let go of the chieftain!

18:16.700 --> 18:17.400
Satoshi!

18:19.200 --> 18:19.740
No!

18:20.240 --> 18:21.490
But Satoshi...!

18:21.700 --> 18:24.200
It's too dangerous. We'll go to Ippei.

18:24.790 --> 18:25.540
But...

18:25.540 --> 18:26.870
Never mind that; hurry!

18:29.330 --> 18:30.040
Satoshi...

18:31.290 --> 18:31.880
Gekkouga,

18:32.590 --> 18:33.630
Water Shuriken!

18:37.170 --> 18:39.470
Fushigibana, Razor Leaf!

18:43.390 --> 18:45.020
Seed Bomb, Yanakkie!

18:45.430 --> 18:47.100
Hiyakkie, Ice Beam!

19:01.490 --> 19:03.950
I won't let you go any farther.

19:06.870 --> 19:09.250
They seem to be in the middle of something.

19:09.540 --> 19:11.000
I don't get what's going on, but...

19:11.460 --> 19:13.000
Oh well, isn't this convenient for us?

19:13.000 --> 19:16.000
It sure is! Let's take advantage of this and make them ours!

19:17.880 --> 19:18.630
A Hiyakkie,

19:18.840 --> 19:19.550
a Yanakkie,

19:19.550 --> 19:23.680
a Gekkouga and a Fushigibana are there! There's lots of them!

19:24.510 --> 19:26.810
All right, let's get them quickly!

19:28.390 --> 19:29.770
Ippei-san, the chieftain...!

19:32.190 --> 19:32.730
Watch out!

19:33.400 --> 19:34.150
Behind you!

19:40.450 --> 19:41.570
Rocket Gang!

19:50.460 --> 19:54.840
A mysterious corps has suddenly appeared in the peaceful Ninja Village.

19:56.840 --> 19:59.630
What is their goal?

20:01.010 --> 20:04.390
And what will Chieftain Hanzo's fate be?

20:05.970 --> 20:09.520
This tale will continue in the next episode!

20:15.900 --> 20:20.940
Sunday December 6th at 8am!

20:16.440 --> 20:18.780
Bambino perform a Pokémon Danson!

20:19.030 --> 20:20.530
On Sunday at 8am!

20:23.990 --> 20:25.990
PokéLove TV!

20:26.160 --> 20:30.540
All right, here comes PokéLove TV, which spreads the charm of Pokémon to the world!

20:30.700 --> 20:32.000
The hosts are me, Ken, and...

20:32.000 --> 20:33.960
Hi! I'm Jenny, nice to meet you!

20:33.960 --> 20:38.380
Today we'll present the Keromousse the Bubble Frog Pokémon Keromatsu has around its neck.

20:38.380 --> 20:40.960
So that's mousse! I thought it was a scarf!

20:40.960 --> 20:43.880
Hey, hey! Keromousse is very useful, you know!

20:41.630 --> 20:51.810
Note that Keromousse is not a move

20:43.880 --> 20:45.300
It can immobilize opponents...

20:45.300 --> 20:47.260
...or serve as a makeshift cushion or rubber band.

20:47.260 --> 20:49.260
You can even make clones with it!

20:49.260 --> 20:51.180
Oh my, that's so economical!

20:51.180 --> 20:53.640
Look at this persistent mud stain!

20:53.640 --> 20:55.270
No way! It's squeaky clean!

20:55.270 --> 20:56.610
All right, I've decided!

20:56.610 --> 20:57.110
Huh?

20:57.310 --> 21:00.860
I'm gonna catch lots of Keromatsu, sell their Keromousse and become filthy rich!

21:00.860 --> 21:03.400
You sound almost like the Rocket Gang!

21:03.400 --> 21:06.030
Ken, wouldn't it be wonderful if it was used like this?

21:09.870 --> 21:13.710
Wow, it's the greatest, Jenny!

21:13.710 --> 21:15.370
Ken!

21:18.130 --> 21:20.000
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:20.210 --> 21:21.340
Towards our next adventure!

21:22.670 --> 21:28.390
After a mysterious ninja corps had kidnapped Hanzo-san we went to save him, but we were ambushed by the enemy.

21:28.970 --> 21:30.350
Gekogashira, let's go!

21:32.350 --> 21:33.060
Gekogashira...?

21:33.560 --> 21:34.640
That light is...!

21:35.520 --> 21:38.690
